        "name": "preamp_stage",
        "description": "NE5532 dual operational amplifier used as the low-level preamplifier domain for the compact audio amplifier. This module accepts the external audio input, applies the primary voltage gain needed toward the overall 100x-200x target, and drives the downstream LM386 input through an analog interstage signal path. The design brief requires the NE5532 output to feed the LM386 input; one amplifier channel is planned as the active preamplifier signal path, while the second channel remains available for optional buffering, filtering, or bias support if later implementation needs it. The device operates from the external single-supply rail and common ground in this project context, so downstream wiring must provide a single-supply operating arrangement and any required input/output biasing networks externally rather than assuming internal midrail generation.",
